Description: The candidate change uses a fresh delivery key per retry attempt.
This breaks gateway deduplication: a timeout after acceptance + retry = two accepted
confirmations for one booking. The fix is to revert to the stable delivery key
stored with the notification.

The defect: on timeout, the gateway has already accepted and recorded the message.
When the sender retries with a NEW key, the gateway treats it as a new message
and accepts it again. Result: two accepted confirmations.

The fix: use notification.deliveryKey (stable, set when the booking was created)
for every attempt. The gateway deduplicates on this key, so retries after timeout
return the existing acceptance.

--- a/src/main/kotlin/com/conferenceplanner/service/NotificationService.kt (candidate)
+++ b/src/main/kotlin/com/conferenceplanner/service/NotificationService.kt (corrected)
@@ dispatch method
-        // Generate a fresh delivery key for each attempt to avoid stale state
-        val attemptDeliveryKey = "confirm-${notification.bookingId}-${UUID.randomUUID()}"
-
-        try {
-            val delivery = deliverToGateway(attemptDeliveryKey, payload)
+        try {
+            val delivery = deliverToGateway(notification.deliveryKey, payload)

(All references to attemptDeliveryKey revert to notification.deliveryKey)
